<article class="env-lemma" id="0EEI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EEI">Lemma <span data-tag="0EEI">110.21.1</span>.</a> There exists a Jacobson, universally catenary, Noetherian domain $B$ with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_1, \mathfrak m_2$ such that $\dim (B_{\mathfrak m_1}) = 1$ and $\dim (B_{\mathfrak m_2}) = 2$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The construction of $B$ is given above. We just point out that $B$ is universally catenary by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NJ" data-tag="00NJ">10.105.4</a> and Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JB" data-tag="02JB">29.17.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>